+## Client attach event hooks
+
+On a host with the `client.attached` capability, a plugin can declare:
+
+```toml
+[[events]]
+on = "client.attached"
+command = ["./bin/my-plugin", "ensure"]
+platforms = ["macos"]
+```
+
+After each successful shell or terminal client registration, the server emits
+one public event and dispatches matching hooks asynchronously through the
+normal plugin runner. Enabled-state and effective-platform filters still apply.
+`HERDR_PLUGIN_EVENT=client.attached`; `HERDR_PLUGIN_EVENT_JSON` contains an
+envelope with `event: "client_attached"` and `data` containing
+`type: "client_attached"`, a server-local numeric `client_id`, and
+`client_kind: "shell"` or `"terminal"`. Subscribe through `events.subscribe`
+using `{"type":"client.attached"}`. API-only requests, failed handshakes, and
+handoff do not trigger this hook; in particular a plugin API probe does not
+launch the plugin itself. Detaching a client does not mean its server died;
+server liveness must be checked separately.
+
+The desktop-pet integration requires the supplied patch against official
+Herdr v0.9.3 (or a future release that explicitly advertises this capability);
+stock v0.9.3 does **not** implement this hook. Check warnings and subscription
+acceptance rather than inferring support from `min_herdr_version`.
+
